── raw route is not an http.Handler
✗ constructor failed

    ✗ raw route is not an http.Handler

    route "POST /uploads", registered by files.notAHandler,
    was given a value of type http_test.notAHandler.

  transport.Raw hands its handler to whichever adapter serves the
  protocol, and this one is HTTP: the value must implement
  net/http.Handler. Wrap a function with http.HandlerFunc(fn).

  A constructor returned this error while the graph for scope "warren/transport/http" was
  being built. Fix the constructor, or the configuration it read.

── conflicting patterns
✗ constructor failed

    ✗ conflicting HTTP route patterns

    pattern "GET /users/{uid}" conflicts with pattern "GET /users/{id}":
GET /users/{uid} matches the same requests as GET /users/{id}

  net/http.ServeMux refuses two patterns that can match the same request,
  because which one wins would be arbitrary. Two routes with
  differently-named wildcards on the same path — "/users/{id}" and
  "/users/{uid}" — are the usual cause: pick one name.

  Both patterns come from a controller's Register method; grep for them.

  A constructor returned this error while the graph for scope "warren/transport/http" was
  being built. Fix the constructor, or the configuration it read.

── routes with no server
✗ registered routes have no adapter serving them

    4 HTTP route(s) — add http.Server(...) to warren.New

  A route nobody serves is a route that silently 404s in production.
